.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt VPS-DEPLOY-STATIC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vps-deploy-static
.Nd build and install the RAILS/__other static brand exports on the production VPS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm all | sommerseth | alfa
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the deploy entry point for the static brand exports at
.Pa RAILS/__other :
.Sy sommerseth
serves thor.brgen.no from /var/www/sommerseth on loopback port 38191 and
.Sy alfa
serves alfa.brgen.no from /var/www/alfa on loopback port 38192, behind the
same relayd TLS termination as the Rails fleet. It is not a
.Xr vps-deploy 8
target: those deploy rcctl-managed Rails apps, and these sites are served by
httpd vhosts with no daemon to restart.
.Pp
Run it on vm23 as the unprivileged account
.Cm dev ,
not as root and not wrapped in
.Xr doas 1 ;
the script escalates only for the individual steps that require it, and root
cannot reach the git remote for the pull that should precede a deploy.
.Pp
For each target the script builds the Next.js export in place (bun with a
frozen lockfile when the box has it, otherwise npm ci), replaces the chroot
tree wholesale — the previous tree is removed first, because a stale hashed
_next chunk that stale HTML still references is exactly the almost-works a
static site must never ship — and then verifies that the loopback vhost
answers and returns the site's title. A green exit therefore means deployed
and serving on loopback, not merely copied. When nothing listens on the
loopback port the failure names the activation steps recorded at the bottom
of OPENBSD/etc/relayd.conf (certificate SANs, config install, restart) rather
than pretending the site is up.
.Pp
The accepted targets are
.Cm all ,
.Cm sommerseth ,
and
.Cm alfa .
Unknown targets are refused before anything is built or copied.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "VPS_STATIC_OUT_SRC"
.It Ev VPS_STATIC_OUT_SRC
Install this ready-made out/ tree instead of building, skipping npm and bun
entirely. The directory must contain index.html. This is the escape hatch for
a box with no node runtime: build on the workstation, ship the tree, rerun.
.It Ev REMOTE_PUB4
Path to the pub4 checkout on the box. The default is /home/dev/pub4.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "1"
.It 0
Every target was built (or installed), installed into the chroot, and answered
on its loopback port with the expected title.
.It 1
At least one target failed; earlier targets that succeeded stay deployed.
.It 2
Usage error, unknown target, or an attempt to run as root.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vps-deploy 8
